    "long_instructions": "You are an archivist standardizing a library’s catalog.\r\n\r\nIn this program, you have an `entries` list of nine catalog entries.  Your task is to complete the `normalize` function. It should return a standardized form for each entry.\r\n\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- Run the program. How many entries does it count? How many different items?\r\n- Implement the first normalization rule: lowercasing text.\r\n- Test your program. It should count seven unique entries.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nRemember you can lowercase `text` with `text.lower()`. Be sure to assign the result back to the `text` variable.\r\n\r\n```python\r\ntext = text.lower()\r\n```",
